<style>
  body {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: #fcfcfb;
    font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;
  }

  #tariff-loop-container {
    position: fixed;
    inset: 0;
  }

  #scene-label {
    position: fixed;
    top: 1.8rem;
    left: 2rem;
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #898781;
    z-index: 10;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  #controls {
    position: fixed;
    bottom: 1.6rem;
    left: 2rem;
    z-index: 20;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    max-width: 270px;
  }

  #controls .hint {
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    color: #898781;
    margin-bottom: 0.3rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  #controls button {
    background: #fcfcfb;
    border: 1px solid #c3c2b7;
    text-align: left;
    font-size: 0.74rem;
    color: #0b0b0b;
    padding: 0.45rem 0.8rem;
    cursor: pointer;
    border-radius: 3px;
  }

  #controls button:hover {
    border-color: #52514e;
  }

  #controls label {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    color: #52514e;
    padding: 0.35rem 0.1rem;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  #controls .reset {
    color: #898781;
    border-style: dashed;
  }

  #legend {
    position: fixed;
    top: 1.6rem;
    right: 2rem;
    z-index: 10;
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    color: #52514e;
    line-height: 1.9;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  #legend .swatch {
    display: inline-block;
    width: 0.7rem;
    height: 0.7rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    margin-right: 0.45rem;
    vertical-align: -0.08rem;
    border: 1.5px solid;
  }

  #legend .sign {
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-right: 0.45rem;
  }

  #story-open {
    position: fixed;
    bottom: 1.8rem;
    right: 2rem;
    z-index: 50;
    background: none;
    border: 1px solid #c3c2b7;
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #898781;
    padding: 0.45rem 0.9rem;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  #story-open:hover {
    color: #0b0b0b;
    border-color: #52514e;
  }

  #story-modal {
    position: fixed;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 100;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    background: rgba(252, 252, 251, 0.88);
    backdrop-filter: blur(3px);
  }

  #story-modal.hidden {
    display: none;
  }

  #story-modal-inner {
    background: #fff;
    border: 1px solid #e1e0d9;
    max-width: 680px;
    width: calc(100% - 3rem);
    max-height: 82vh;
    overflow-y: auto;
    padding: 3rem 3.5rem;
    position: relative;
  }

  #story-modal-inner h1 {
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #0b0b0b;
    margin: 0 0 0.25rem;
  }

  #story-modal-inner .byline {
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    color: #898781;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  #story-modal-inner h2 {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #52514e;
    margin: 1.8rem 0 0.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #f0efec;
    padding-bottom: 0.3rem;
  }

  #story-modal-inner p {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: #52514e;
    margin: 0 0 0.8rem;
  }

  #story-modal-inner a {
    color: #256abf;
  }

  #story-close {
    position: absolute;
    top: 1.2rem;
    right: 1.4rem;
    background: none;
    border: none;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: #898781;
    cursor: pointer;
    line-height: 1;
    padding: 0.2rem 0.4rem;
  }

  #story-close:hover {
    color: #0b0b0b;
  }
</style>

<div id="tariff-loop-container"></div>

<div id="scene-label">Tariff Loop — who paid, who got refunded</div>

<div id="legend">
  <div>
    <span
      class="swatch"
      style="border-color: #2a78d6; background: #2a78d626;"
    ></span>
    state + policy
  </div>
  <div>
    <span
      class="swatch"
      style="border-color: #eb6834; background: #eb683426;"
    ></span>
    market + retail
  </div>
  <div>
    <span
      class="swatch"
      style="border-color: #1baf7a; background: #1baf7a26;"
    ></span>
    households
  </div>
  <div>
    <span
      class="swatch"
      style="border-color: #eda100; background: #eda10026;"
    ></span>
    courts + politics
  </div>
  <div>
    <span
      class="sign"
      style="color: #2a78d6;"
    >+</span>
    same-direction link
  </div>
  <div>
    <span
      class="sign"
      style="color: #e34948;"
    >−</span>
    inverse link
  </div>
</div>

<div id="controls">
  <div class="hint">
    Click the top of any node to push it up, the bottom to push it down, and watch the pulse propagate — like Nicky Case's LOOPY.
    Or replay the actual sequence:
  </div>
  <button id="scenario-1">
    ① Apr 2025 — impose tariffs
  </button>
  <button id="scenario-2">
    ② Feb 2026 — Supreme Court strikes them down
  </button>
  <button id="scenario-3">
    ③ Aug 2026 — $2.9B refund lands at Walmart
  </button>
  <label>
    <input
      type="checkbox"
      id="rebate-toggle"
    />
    Enact the consumer rebate (H.R. 7865 — still just a bill)
  </label>
  <button
    id="sim-reset"
    class="reset"
  >
    reset
  </button>
</div>

<div
  id="story-modal"
  class="hidden"
>
  <div id="story-modal-inner">
    <button
      id="story-close"
      aria-label="Close"
    >
      &times;
    </button>

    <h1>The Tariff Loop</h1>
    <div class="byline">
      Causal feedback model &mdash; August 2026
    </div>

    <p>
      In April 2025 the White House imposed sweeping import duties under IEEPA emergency powers.
      Importers paid roughly $168 billion at the border, and much of it passed through to shelf prices &mdash; about $2,500 per household per year by
      <a
        href="https://www.jec.senate.gov/public/_cache/files/4836e257-91a5-426b-95bb-3e575a855f5b/jec-fact-sheet-on-cost-of-tariffs-for-families-2026.pdf"
        target="_blank"
      >Joint Economic Committee estimates</a>.
    </p>

    <p>
      Higher prices fed legal and political pushback.
      In February 2026 the Supreme Court ruled the tariffs an unlawful use of emergency powers, and in May the government began refunding the $168 billion &mdash; to the roughly 330,000 <em>importers</em> who wrote the checks, not to the consumers who ultimately paid.
    </p>

    <p>
      This week (August 20, 2026) Walmart reported its $2.9 billion refund and said it would use it to temporarily lower prices on 11,000 items
      (<a
        href="https://www.cnn.com/2026/08/20/business/walmart-tariff-refund"
        target="_blank"
      >CNN</a>,
      <a
        href="https://www.nbcnews.com/business/consumer/walmart-earnings-tariffs-sales-growth-rcna593450"
        target="_blank"
      >NBC</a>,
      <a
        href="https://www.cbsnews.com/news/walmart-tariff-refunds-lower-prices/"
        target="_blank"
      >CBS</a>,
      <a
        href="https://fortune.com/2026/08/20/walmart-tariff-refunds-prices/"
        target="_blank"
      >Fortune</a>).
      Target received $994M, Home Depot $730M, TJX $331M, Lowe's $80M.
      Goldman Sachs expects prices to fall far more slowly than they rose.
    </p>

    <h2>The three loops</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>B &mdash; relief loop (balancing).</strong>
      Prices &rarr; pushback &rarr; courts &rarr; tariff rate (&minus;).
      The system self-corrects, but with a year of lag.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>R &mdash; rollback loop (reinforcing).</strong>
      Refunds &rarr; margins &rarr; rollbacks &rarr; prices (&minus;) &rarr; budgets &rarr; demand &rarr; margins.
      The refund only reaches households if retailers choose to route it through prices &mdash; and rollbacks are partial, temporary, and double as a market-share weapon.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>The missing arc.</strong>
      The dashed line from refunds to household budgets is the
      <a
        href="https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/7865/all-info"
        target="_blank"
      >American Consumer Tariff Rebate Act</a> &mdash; a direct-payment path that exists on paper but has not become law.
      Toggle it on to see how the loop would close.
    </p>

    <h2>Why "kickback"</h2>
    <p>
      The money flowed consumers &rarr; retailers &rarr; Treasury, but refunds flow Treasury &rarr; retailers &rarr; stop.
      The asymmetry is structural: the legal claim belongs to whoever paid the duty at the border, not whoever paid it at the register.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<button id="story-open">The story</button>

<script>
  window.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded", () => {
    const sim = window.tariffLoop();

    document.getElementById("scenario-1").addEventListener("click", () => sim.inject("tariff", +1));
    document.getElementById("scenario-2").addEventListener("click", () => sim.inject("scotus", +1));
    document.getElementById("scenario-3").addEventListener("click", () => sim.inject("refunds", +1));
    document.getElementById("sim-reset").addEventListener("click", () => sim.reset());
    document.getElementById("rebate-toggle").addEventListener("change", (e) => sim.setRebate(e.target.checked));

    const modal = document.getElementById("story-modal");
    document.getElementById("story-open").addEventListener("click", () => modal.classList.remove("hidden"));
    document.getElementById("story-close").addEventListener("click", () => modal.classList.add("hidden"));
    document.addEventListener("keydown", (e) => {
      if (e.key === "Escape") modal.classList.add("hidden");
    });
  });
</script>
